n/math-academy-id "q-112328" :question/problem "Use Pascal's triangle to determine the value of $(\\frac{2}{1}).$" :question/worked-solution "To find the value of $(\\frac{2}{1}),$ we need to find the number that is located in row $2$ and position $1$ of Pascal's triangle. \n\n**Important**: When counting the rows and positions in Pascal's triangle, we always start counting from zero! Remember:\n\n- The top row of Pascal's triangle is row $0.$\n\n- The first position of each row (the one of the left) is position number $0.$\n\nThe value located in row $2$ and position $1$ is highlighted below.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} &  &  &  &  & 1 \\\\  &  &  &  & 1 &  & 1 \\\\  &  &  & 1 &  & 2 &  & 1 \\\\  &  & 1 &  & 3 &  & 3 &  & 1 \\\\  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $(\\frac{2}{1})=2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-112328/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "be11193b-a241-5812-a1c1-54d233ae9ddd"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-112328"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-112325/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer/id #uuid "7cd38594-9c75-5d19-ad00-5ca0efa8186c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-112325/selection/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53" :answer/id #uuid "7b754b8b-4181-58d1-aec1-0217d8b7a23d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-112325/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "73a06fde-a74c-5b0b-89d7-b7eeb00f268c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-112325/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "7d0ac021-c519-543b-906b-d44e3ec7d76c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ens