f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" "q-112329/selection/66dedd51c696580d351ab6a45c1c63cb495081ccf219c3c3c62f1d90fbeb5a49"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-112329" :question/id #uuid "5deb48f3-1beb-5d95-8f36-d7d4c47e7bec" :question/math-academy-id "q-112329" :question/problem "Use Pascal's triangle to determine the value of $(\\frac{6}{1}).$" :question/worked-solution "To find the value of $(\\frac{6}{1}),$ we need to find the number that is located in row $6$ and position $1$ of Pascal's triangle. \n\n**Important**: When counting the rows and positions in Pascal's triangle, we always start counting from zero! Remember:\n\n- The top row of Pascal's triangle is row $0.$\n\n- The first position of each row (the one of the left) is position number $0.$\n\nThe value located in row $6$ and position $1$ is highlighted below.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} &  &  &  &  &  &  & 1 \\\\  &  &  &  &  &  & 1 &  & 1 \\\\  &  &  &  &  & 1 &  & 2 &  & 1 \\\\  &  &  &  & 1 &  & 3 &  & 3 &  & 1 \\\\  &  &  & 1 &  & 4 &  & 6 &  & 4 &  & 1 \\\\  &  & 1 &  & 5 &  & 10 &  & 10 &  & 5 &  & 1 \\\\  & 1 &  & 6 &  & 15 &  & 20 &  & 15 &  & 6 &  & 1 \\\\ ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $(\\frac{6}{1})=6.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-112329/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "be11193b-a241-5812-a1c1-54d233ae9ddd"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-112329"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-69718/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "0dd24b6d-59e9-53ee-be23-2a48d271610e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-69718/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "316b8809-c323-59fd-8c7e-3fd4b2387cee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/en