f-6765-5a4f-8c3e-2a8b1f16c318" :question/math-academy-id "q-113620" :question/problem "Determine the value of $(\\frac{7}{2}).$" :question/worked-solution "The binomial coefficient $(\\frac{n}{r})$ is given by the formula\n\n$$\n(\\frac{n}{r})=\\frac{n!}{(n-r)!\\,r!}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have $n=7$ and $r=2.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\frac{7}{2}) & =\\frac{7!}{(7-2)!\\cdot 2!} \\\\  & =\\frac{7\\cdot 6\\cdot 5!}{5!\\cdot 2!} \\\\  & =\\frac{7\\cdot 6\\cdot \\cancel{5!}}{\\cancel{5!}\\cdot 2} \\\\  & =\\frac{42}{2} \\\\  & =21.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-113620/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e5c108c0-f32a-5725-af3b-c3e747da09f2"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-113620"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-113613/selection/772faee3af740960f7d296ca245df4da797a9e413368076cbaa828915d92739d" :answer/id #uuid "55d37008-3ded-55ad-9b46-a0336f626e59" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "128" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-113613/selection/ad7a3824e2b90d316aedd9968e2fdff13c67ee5110546b7a43eeb384aa267fd0" :answer/id #uuid "3925c0be-3ce4-5582-a3ae-3d6e18a0403d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "112" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-113613/selection/a20b3c9808c291c56ec5bfc5f0f93a856fc692714ca7ebd36c5e4bc361f7075c" :answer/id #uuid "808587d7-c3b5-51f0-9f11-cfbce73229e3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "42" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-113613/selection/879a225aaf1b8272157c33247ace982b7e338d5701ba0d4d6c31dd38d4da6784" :answer/id #uuid "145b8110-f8c7-5a72-a618-8f189015cd2a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "56" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-113613/selection/0674b229b15216f6ea870ccaaf87984357f5d6af66421aad0753c15d921d419a" :answer/id #uuid "cb4ec934-95fd-57ba-931e-73fadb7310f1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "64" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-113613/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "833d3b40-41e0-5da0-9986-f9afddf1b372" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-113613/selection/879a225aaf1b8272157c33247ace982b7e338d5701ba0d4d6c31dd38d4da6784" :answer-field/choices ["q-113613/selection/772faee3af740960f7d296ca245df4da797a9e413368076cbaa828915d92739d" "q-113613/selection/ad7a3824e2b90d316aedd9968e2fdff13c67ee5110546b7a43eeb384aa267fd0" "q-113613/selection/a20b3c9808c291c56ec5bfc5f0f93a856fc692714ca7ebd36c5e4bc361f7075c" "q-113613/selection/879a225aaf1b8272157c33247ace982b7e338d5701ba0d4d6c31dd38d4da6784" "q-113613/selection/0674b229b15216f6ea870ccaaf87984357f5d6af66421aad0753c15d921d419a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-113613" :question/id #uuid "b955a904-102b-509c-b6fe-26db40c4d90a" :question/math-academy-id "q-113613" :question/problem "Determine the value of $(\\frac{8}{5}).$" :question/worked-solution "The binomial coefficient $(\\frac{n}{r})$ is given by the formula\n\n$$\n(\\frac{n}{r})=\\frac{n!}{(n-r)!\\,r!}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have $n=8$ and $r=5.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\frac{8}{5}) & =\\frac{8!}{(8-5)!\\cdot 5!} \\\\  & =\\frac{8\\cdot 7\\cdot 6\\cdot 5!}{3!\\cdot 5!} \\\\  & =\\frac{8\\cdot 7\\cdot 6\\cdot 5!}{6\\cdot 5!} \\\\  & =\\frac{8\\cdot 7\\cdot \\cancel{6}\\cdot \\cancel{5!}}{\\cancel{6}\\cdot \\cancel{5!}} \\\\  & =8\\cdot 7 \\\\  & =56.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-113613/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e5c108c0-f32a-5725-af3b-c3e747da09f2"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-113613"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-5108"] :question/problem "Use Pascal's triangle to determine the value of $\\displaystyle{3 \\choose 2}.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the value of $\\displaystyle{\\color{red}{3} \\choose {\\color{blue}2}},$ we need to find the number that is located in row $\\color{red}3$ and position $\\color{blue}2$ of Pascal's triangle. \n\n**Important:** Remember that when counting the rows and positions in Pascal's triangle, we always start counting from zero!\n\n- The top row of Pascal's triangle is row $0.$\n\n- The first position of each row (the one of the left) is position number $0.$\n\nThe value located in row $\\color{red}3$ and position $\\color{blue}2$ is highlighted below.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} &  &  &  & 1 \\\\  &  &  & 1 &  & 1 \\\\  &  & 1 &  & 2 &  & 1 \\\\  & 1 &  & 3 &  & 3 &  & 1 \\\\ ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\displaystyle{3 \\choose 2} = 3.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-5109"] :question/problem "Which expression is missing in the following equation?\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle{4 \\choose 3} = \\displaystyle{3 \\choose 2} + \\displaystyle{\\left[ \\phantom{3 \\choose 3}\\right]}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To find $\\displaystyle{\\color{red}{4} \\choose {\\color{blue}3}},$ we need to find the number that is located in row $\\color{red}4$ and position $\\color{blue}3$ of Pascal's triangle. \n\n**Important:** Remember that when counting the rows and positions in Pascal's triangle, we always start counting from zero!\n\n- The top row of Pascal's triangle is row $0.$\n\n- The first position of each row (the one of the left) is position number $0.$\n\nThe location of $\\displaystyle{4 \\choose 3}$ in Pascal's triangle is highlighted below.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} &  &  &  &  &  &  & (\\frac{0}{0}) \\\\  &  &  &  &  &  & (\\frac{1}{0}) &  & (\\frac{1}{1}) \\\\  &  &  &  &  & (\\frac{2}{0}) &  & (\\frac{2}{1}) &  & (\\frac{2}{2}) \\\\  &  &  &  & (\\frac{3}{0}) &  & (\\frac{3}{1}) &  & (\\frac{3}{2}) &  & (\\frac{3}{3}) \\\\  &  &  & (\\frac{4}{0}) &  & (\\frac{4}{1}) &  & (\\frac{4}{2}) &  & (\\frac{4}{3}) &  & (\\frac{4}{4}) \\\\  &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, $\\displaystyle{4 \\choose 3}$ is the sum of the two closest numbers located in the previous row. So\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle{4 \\choose 3} = \\displaystyle{3 \\choose 2} + \\displaystyle{3 \\choose 3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing expression is $\\displaystyle{3 \\choose 3}.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-5231"] :question/problem "Determine the value of $\\displaystyle{5 \\choose 4}.$" :question/worked-solution "The binomial coefficient $\\displaystyle{n \\choose r}$ is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle{n \\choose r} = \\dfrac{n!}{(n-r)!\\,  r!}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have $n = 5$ and $r = 4.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\frac{5}{4}) & =\\frac{5!}{(5-4)!\\cdot 4!} \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\cdot 4!}{1!\\cdot 4!} \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\cdot \\cancel{4!}}{1\\cdot \\cancel{4!}} \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
